   174	## Appendix Z: superseded draft (2026-11-05T22:58Z, budget lever; not scheduled)
   175	> # Plan 007: time-aware budget lever (pre-registered 2026-11-05T22:58Z; CANDIDATE, not runnable; first quality lever after report 010, dec 039 item 2)
   176	> Evidence: results/failure_taxonomy_e4b_v001_v5.json (n=8, e4b-v001, cap 1.4 min, ungraded): 4/8 hit the session timeout
   177	> without calling submit_patch (1 of these made zero edits, so its patch was empty); the finalization diff rescued a non-empty patch in 3 of the 4.
   178	> The short cap inflates the timeout rate. Re-measure the base rate at the candidate cap before trusting the size of the effect.
   179	> Lever: the bundle prompt (and a skill if needed) sets a step budget: first source edit by ~50% of the budget, run the targeted
   180	> test, then submit_patch before the cap. The agent probably can't see wall-clock time from inside a declarative ADK bundle, so the
   181	> budget is stated in LLM-call/tool-call counts derived from the measured calls-per-minute at the target cap (v5: ~9-16 LLM calls
   182	> at 1.4 min). Check what the agent can observe before building. No repo-specific content.
   183	> Hypothesis: B reduces timeout-without-submit and zero-edit outcomes and does not lower the pass rate (it may raise it slightly).
   184	> Expected effect: primary = pass rate, +0 to +3 tasks on 33 dev (small; most timeouts are already rescued by the finalization diff);
   185	> secondary = timeout-without-submit rate (expect at least halved), zero-edit/empty-patch rate, submitted-but-unverified rate (risk: an early submit
   186	> skips the test run).
   187	> Design: paired, same 33 dev ids, k=2 seeds each, same model and cap (the cap of the then-current best bundle), A = current best,
   188	> B = A + budget prompt only (byte diff limited to prompts/). Interaction with plan 005 (dec 022 item 4 empty-patch protection):
   189	> run as a 2x2 sharing arm A if compute allows (A, A+005, A+007, A+005+007); otherwise 005 first, then 007 on top of the winner.
   190	> Decision rule: adopt B if B-only > A-only with exact sign test p < 0.2 and no rise in timeouts; if p >= 0.2 but the timeout-without-
   191	> submit rate falls by >= 50% with no pass-rate loss (B-only >= A-only), adopt B as a safety change; else keep A.
   192	> Compute: local paired quality eval (GPU), not authorized; request it in the report that follows report 010. Timing re-check is only needed if
   193	> call counts change materially (not expected, since the cap is unchanged).
